  "notes": "Craven Avenue runs along the plate's top neat line east of Langland Avenue; only a 20-30 ft sliver shows, so its two crossings are at the plate edge (y is the middle of the visible sliver). Thompson Heights Avenue: name printed as THOMPSON HEIGHTS along the diagonal part west of the strip and AVENUE near x 7000. Langland Avenue continues south of Thompson Heights Avenue 60 ft wide, then as a 30 ft strip past Glen Parker Avenue. Fergus Street at the top is a 30 ft strip along the boundary. '?' at Haight (5663,2910): 60 ft street from Hamilton Avenue, printed only AVENUE (possibly Bruce Avenue). '?' at Donaldson Place: 50 ft avenue running north from Pullan Avenue on the line of Langland Avenue, printed only AVE. (probably North Argyle); it is the north arm of the Langland/Pullan crossing. Pullan Avenue east of Hamilton: name printed only west of Hamilton; it jogs about 20 px at Langland. Chase Avenue (bottom edge): printed only AVENUE east of the strip; name taken from the plate description. Bruce Avenue here is a detached piece closed at both ends."
